      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ah",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1390822908,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 135757555,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793600000000,
      "created": 1793600000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to roll out safely?\n- batches with maxSurge / maxUnavailable, minReadySeconds\n- waves to limit blast radius, bake time between waves\n- health gate on business metrics, compare with old version\n- auto rollback in our own Rollout Controller (K8s progressDeadline doesn't roll back)\n\n2. How to make health checks accurate?\n- readiness checks only the instance itself, not shared dependencies\n- local probes + external LB checks\n- node failure vs network partition: mass heartbeat loss -> slow down eviction\n\n3. What if the control plane fails?\n- controllers: multiple replicas + leader lease, progress persisted per batch\n- static stability: agent runs from local cache\n- stateful: recreate only after old instance confirmed gone (or fencing)\n\n4. How to scale to 10k nodes?\n- cell-based: one control plane + etcd per cell, global orchestrator on top\n- lightweight lease heartbeat, status only on change\n- regional image cache + P2P, pre-pull before the next batch",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to roll out safely?\n- batches with maxSurge / maxUnavailable, minReadySeconds\n- waves to limit blast radius, bake time between waves\n- health gate on business metrics, compare with old version\n- auto rollback in our own Rollout Controller (K8s progressDeadline doesn't roll back)\n\n2. How to make health checks accurate?\n- readiness checks only the instance itself, not shared dependencies\n- local probes + external LB checks\n- node failure vs network partition: mass heartbeat loss -> slow down eviction\n\n3. What if the control plane fails?\n- controllers: multiple replicas + leader lease, progress persisted per batch\n- static stability: agent runs from local cache\n- stateful: recreate only after old instance confirmed gone (or fencing)\n\n4. How to scale to 10k nodes?\n- cell-based: one control plane + etcd per cell, global orchestrator on top\n- lightweight lease heartbeat, status only on change\n- regional image cache + P2P, pre-pull before the next batch",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
